        "original_id": "20e57698-98bb-54a6-acca-f8e54afeefc0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Goose Rocks Beach\n- People: Eliot O'Hara\n- Organizations: O'Hara Watercolor School\n- Events: Great Fires of 1947\n\nFacts:\n- From 1930 to 1947, the O'Hara Watercolor School operated at Goose Rocks Beach under American watercolor painter Eliot O'Hara.\n- In 1947, the Great Fires of 1947 burned down the O'Hara Watercolor School and many other buildings at Goose Rocks Beach.\n- In 1947, the Great Fires of 1947 collectively killed 16 people.",
